<title>TAIWAN: China Steel July pre-tax up 20 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Steel July pre-tax up 20 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Steel Corp, Taiwan's largest steel maker, said on Friday it posted a pre-tax profit of T$1.814 billion in July, up 20 percent from T$1.511 billion in July 1996.</p>
<p>The firm has adopted a fiscal year starting every July 1. Its July sales rose to T$8.71 billion from T$7.22 billion a year earlier, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>China Steel, previously state-run, was privatised in April 1995.</p>
